(BAS-29 - the for-loop example, LANGUAGE.md:105:
 `For each number from 1 to 10, print the number, print " ".`
 Both actions belong to the loop, so the separator prints once per
 iteration. Shortened to 1 to 3 so the recorded output stays small.
 `print` appends a newline of its own, so the separator lands on its own
 line - that is Print's documented behaviour (LANGUAGE.md Input/Output),
 not a Basics claim, and the spacing the example implies is only achieved
 with `without newline`. The separator lines below each hold one space.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-29.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   1
    
   2
    
   3
    
)
For each number from 1 to 3, print the number, print " ".
